b947-590d-85bd-cdc2cbb91d09" 13194139533891 true] [17592186263970 1145 "First, let $u=5-2x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{5-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5-2x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the above by writing $C=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K$ for another arbitrary constant $K,$ and then we can combine the two terms using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5-2x|+C & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5-2x|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5-2x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡K) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|5-2x|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we finally conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{5-2x}\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|5-2x|).\n$$" 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263972 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263973 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263974 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263975 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263976 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1041 "selection" 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263973 13194139533891 true] [17592186263971 1110 #uuid "4e1ccc23-99eb-55f9-bc95-8ad5450e4e06" 13194139533891 true] [17592186263972 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|5-2x|)" 13194139533891 true] [17592186263972 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533891 true] [1759218